Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Campaign saves v71: TestCamp.cam decodes end to end
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Normal in-campaign saves (gCampDataVersion 71) now fully decode:
- unit_decoder: v71 layout gates (pos_.z_ at v70, ushort
  current_wp/wp_count at v71, squadron stores[220], flight v>65
  trio, package small/big branch by unit_flags & U_FINAL) +
  class-table dispatch replicating FreeFalcon's NewUnit, with a
  hardened trial-and-error fallback. TestCamp: 1715/1715 units,
  cursor-exact at 423,065 bytes.
- team_decoder: full rewrite — correct 739-byte TeamClass (Team is
  uchar; the old 52-byte read garbled every slot), ATM with airbase
  schedules + ATO mission-request worklist, GTM/NTM skips.
- campaign_decoder: full .cmp walk (timers, ratios, event queues,
  camp map, squadron preload, creator block) — 22,080/22,080.
- objective_decoder: version param, VU_ID order fixed (num first),
  new decode_obd for the delta records normal saves carry.
- world_json/cam2json: objective base+delta merge with auto-discovery
  (sibling .obj else the bundled save1.obj fixture), --objectives;
  emits ids, flight/package mission data, team ATM requests,
  campaign events. CamArchive remembers its source path so the
  world viewer's import flow gets all of this in-process.
- kunsan_campaign.world.json: the never-committed CampaignTick
  fixture, regenerated (scripts/make_kunsan_fixture.py) — main was
  RED on 6 tests, now 1857/1857.
